From: Mark Harfouche <mark.harfouche@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] python: fix building the bindings with Py_LIMITED_API >= 3.11

From Py_LIMITED_API 0x030b0000 on, CPython stops defining several object
helpers as casting macros and provides only static inline functions
taking PyObject* (see Include/object.h). Three spots in OpenCV relied on
the old macros:

1. pycompat.hpp: CPython no longer defines PyType_CheckExact as a macro,
   so OpenCV's `#ifndef PyType_CheckExact` fallback is used. That fallback
   names its parameter `obj` but expands `Py_TYPE(op)`:

     cv2.cpp:306:10: error: use of undeclared identifier 'op'

2. cv2_convert.cpp: NumPy's PyArray_GETCONTIGUOUS passes its
   PyArrayObject* argument straight to Py_INCREF, which now only accepts
   PyObject*:

     cv2_convert.cpp:236:42: error: cannot convert 'PyArrayObject*' to
     'PyObject*'

   Expand the macro with an explicit cast; behaviour is unchanged.

3. cv2_convert.cpp / cv2_numpy.cpp: the bfloat16 / float8 dtype support
   added in 5.1 calls Py_INCREF on a PyArray_Descr*:

     cv2_numpy.cpp:49:19: error: cannot convert 'PyArray_Descr*' to
     'PyObject*'

   Cast to PyObject*; behaviour is unchanged.

conda-forge builds the cv2 bindings with -DPYTHON3_LIMITED_API=ON on
python_min, which moved from 3.10 to 3.11. Not yet fixed upstream on
opencv 4.x or 5.x as of 2026-11.
---
 modules/python/src2/cv2_convert.cpp | 9 +++++++--
 modules/python/src2/cv2_numpy.cpp   | 2 +-
 modules/python/src2/pycompat.hpp    | 2 +-
 3 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
diff --git a/modules/python/src2/cv2_convert.cpp b/modules/python/src2/cv2_convert.cpp
index 503c19f..79200e2 100644
--- a/modules/python/src2/cv2_convert.cpp
+++ b/modules/python/src2/cv2_convert.cpp
@@ -247,7 +247,12 @@ bool pyopencv_to(PyObject* o, Mat& m, const ArgInfo& info)
             oarr = (PyArrayObject*) o;
         }
         else {
-            oarr = PyArray_GETCONTIGUOUS(oarr);
+            // Expanded PyArray_GETCONTIGUOUS: with Py_LIMITED_API >= 3.11,
+            // Py_INCREF no longer casts its argument to PyObject*.
+            if (PyArray_ISCONTIGUOUS(oarr))
+                Py_INCREF((PyObject*) oarr);
+            else
+                oarr = (PyArrayObject*) PyArray_Copy(oarr);
             o = (PyObject*) oarr;
         }
 
@@ -389,7 +394,7 @@ PyObject* pyopencv_from(const cv::Mat& m)
     {
         PyArray_Descr* descr = exotic;
         if( descr )
-            Py_INCREF(descr);
+            Py_INCREF((PyObject*) descr);
         else
             descr = PyArray_DescrFromType(cvDepthToNumpyType(m.depth()));
         return pyopencv_from_new_array(m, descr);
diff --git a/modules/python/src2/cv2_numpy.cpp b/modules/python/src2/cv2_numpy.cpp
index 2895c17..b83abb2 100644
--- a/modules/python/src2/cv2_numpy.cpp
+++ b/modules/python/src2/cv2_numpy.cpp
@@ -46,7 +46,7 @@ UMatData* NumpyAllocator::allocate(int dims0, const int* sizes, int type, void*
     PyArray_Descr* exotic = nonConventionalDescrForCvDepth(depth);
     if( exotic )
     {
-        Py_INCREF(exotic);  // PyArray_NewFromDescr steals the reference
+        Py_INCREF((PyObject*) exotic);  // PyArray_NewFromDescr steals the reference
         PyObject* eo = PyArray_NewFromDescr(&PyArray_Type, exotic, dims, _sizes.data(),
                                             nullptr, nullptr, 0, nullptr);
         if(!eo)
diff --git a/modules/python/src2/pycompat.hpp b/modules/python/src2/pycompat.hpp
index c936f5e..5a641a1 100644
--- a/modules/python/src2/pycompat.hpp
+++ b/modules/python/src2/pycompat.hpp
@@ -64,7 +64,7 @@
 #endif // PY_MAJOR >=3
 
 #ifndef PyType_CheckExact
-#define PyType_CheckExact(obj) (Py_TYPE(op) == &PyType_Type)
+#define PyType_CheckExact(obj) (Py_TYPE(obj) == &PyType_Type)
 #endif // !PyType_CheckExact
 
 static inline bool getUnicodeString(PyObject * obj, std::string &str)
-- 
2.43.2

